# This repository is a fork of the Entire CLI, a Go project. Vercel only ever
# deploys the static showcase in public/ (see vercel.json outputDirectory).
#
# api/ is the load-bearing entry here: Vercel treats a top-level api/ directory
# as serverless functions and tries to build api/checkpoint/*.go with the Go
# runtime, which fails and takes the whole deployment with it. outputDirectory
# does not prevent that, because function detection runs independently of the
# build output. Excluding the directory is what stops it.
api/

# The rest of the Go tree and toolchain — never needed to serve a static page,
# and excluding it keeps the upload small and the build unambiguous.
cmd/
internal/
e2e/
redact/
perf/
tools/
scripts/
mise-tasks/
docs/
*.go
go.mod
go.sum
mise.toml
.golangci.yaml
.goreleaser*.yaml

# Project code and data, unrelated to the static showcase.
warden/
databricks/
migrations/

# Local and CI noise.
.entire/
.github/
.devcontainer/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.opencode/
.pi/
.vscode/
.ferrata/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
